 "result_text": "`idna.decode(b'\\x8d\\xd2')` now raises `idna.IDNAError` (\"Invalid ASCII in A-label\") instead of `UnicodeDecodeError`. I checked three inputs by hand:\n\n- `b'\\x8d\\xd2'` and `b'xn--\\x8d'` raise `IDNAError`.\n- `b'xn--a'` also raises `IDNAError`; that error came from the existing label check, not from the new punycode handling.\n\nI didn't run the test suite.\n\nThe fix is in `idna/core.py`:\n- **`encode()` and `decode()`:** a non-ASCII `bytes` or `bytearray` input is caught and re-raised as `IDNAError`. `encode()` had the same crash, so I fixed it too.\n- **`ulabel()`:** the punycode decode and the ASCII decode of a label are wrapped the same way, so malformed labels give `IDNAError` too.\n\nI haven't checked every other call in the package that decodes bytes.",
